response:
 The area of the parallelogram is equal to the base $\|\mathbf{v}\|$ times the corresponding height, which is the length of the projection of $\mathbf{w}$ onto
$\mathbf{n} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix},$ the normal vector of the parallelogram.
Let $P$ be the intersection of $\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}$ and the line through $\mathbf{0}$ and $\mathbf{n}.$  Then $\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w} - P = t \mathbf{n}$ for some scalar $t,$ so
\[\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} - (t, 7t) = t \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}.\]Hence, $-1 - t = t(-1)$ and $7 - 7t = t(7),$ so $t = 2.$

